       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Batting Coach Sitanshu Kotak Hails Naman Dhir as Promising Talent</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>India's batting coach Sitanshu Kotak has lauded Naman Dhir following his match-winning performances in T20I series against New Zealand and the West Indies. Dhir secured a victory against New Zealand with an unbeaten 42 off 15 balls and contributed a crucial 24 off six balls against the West Indies, proving his utility as a finisher.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/batting-coach-sitanshu-kotak-hails-naman-dhir-as-promising-t.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Kotak highlighted Dhir's versatility, noting his potential as an off-spinner and his strength as a fielder. Emphasizing Dhir's power-hitting ability and tactical awareness, the coach described the nine-match veteran as a highly promising talent capable of executing specific roles in high-pressure international cricket.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the source's key points regarding the coach's assessment and the player's performance.</p>
