       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi High Court to Rule on Neha Bora Plea</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Delhi High Court is set to issue a ruling regarding a plea filed by Neha Bora, who is challenging a police notice demanding she furnish a peace bond. The case centers on the legal validity and justification for police requiring individuals to sign such bonds during protest-related investigations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/delhi-high-court-to-rule-on-neha-bora-plea.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This legal proceeding has drawn attention to the broader investigative actions taken by Delhi police concerning recent protests. The court's upcoming decision is expected to clarify the legal standards for police intervention and the requirements imposed on citizens to maintain peace.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise and accurately reflects the limited information provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
