     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Crictracker, ESPN Cricinfo">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Harry Brook Defends Team Selection After England ODI Loss</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>England captain Harry Brook defended the decision to omit spinner Adil Rashid for the ODI against Sri Lanka in Rawalpindi, despite England failing to defend a total of 429. Liam Dawson, who replaced Rashid, recorded figures of 1 for 71, which Brook described as the best performance among the bowlers.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/harry-brook-defends-team-selection-after-england-odi-loss.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sri Lanka successfully chased 430, marking the second-highest run-chase in ODI history. Although Brook scored 202, setting a record for England's fastest ODI double century, he stated his individual performance was irrelevant due to the loss. Former captain Nasser Hussain noted the team's ongoing struggle to secure wickets in the middle overs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, balanced, and incorporates the provided figures and external context correctly.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/brook-defends-decision-to-leave-out-adil-rashid-after-england-fail-to-defend-429-against-sri-lanka-2908/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1559759.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>This brief was written from the original report. The same event was independently covered by the other outlets listed here.</p>
    </div>
       
