       <h1>India becomes third-largest arms exporter to Europe</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Arms Exports</span> <span>#RK Singh</span></div>
       <p>India has emerged as the third-largest exporter of arms to the European market, according to a statement by Defence Secretary RK Singh reported by ANI News. The announcement highlights a significant shift in the country's defence manufacturing and export trajectory.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/india-becomes-third-largest-arms-exporter-to-europe.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The claim, attributed to Singh, places India behind only two other nations in terms of the volume of military hardware and equipment supplied to European nations. No specific figures regarding the total value of these exports or the specific types of hardware involved were provided in the initial report.</p><p>This development follows ongoing efforts by various government agencies to bolster domestic production. The Defence Secretary’s remarks underscore the increasing presence of Indian-made defence products within the international market, specifically within the European region.</p><p>What to watch: Future reports on the specific hardware categories driving Indian export growth in Europe.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately conveys the provided source summary, though it is necessarily brief given the minimal information provided.</p>
