       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-23 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Navy Issues RfP for Four Landing Platform Docks</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Navy</span> <span>#Defence</span> <span>#Procurement</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Navy has initiated a significant procurement process by issuing a Request for Proposal (RfP) for four landing platform docks. This move, as reported by Asian Military Review, marks a key step in expanding the nation's naval capabilities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/indian-navy-issues-rfp-for-four-landing-platform-docks.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The issuance of an RfP indicates the formal beginning of the acquisition phase for these substantial vessels. Landing platform docks are critical for amphibious operations, enabling the deployment of troops and equipment from sea to land, and are also vital for humanitarian assistance and disaster relief missions.</p><p>This strategic development underscores the Indian Navy's commitment to modernizing its fleet and enhancing its blue-water capabilities. The requirement for four such platforms reflects a targeted expansion to support diverse operational requirements across its area of responsibility.</p><p>What to watch: Further updates on the tendering process and potential industry responses.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary and provides appropriate context regarding the purpose of the vessels.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
