     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-23 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ishan Kishan ruled out of second T20I against New Zealand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Team India</span> <span>#BCCI</span></div>
       <p>Ishan Kishan has been officially ruled out of the second T20I against New Zealand due to a low-grade right adductor strain. The Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) confirmed the injury in a statement on October 23, 2026, noting that Kishan sustained the injury during the first match of the series. The BCCI Medical Team is currently monitoring his progress as the squad prepares for the upcoming fixture at Hagley Oval.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/ishan-kishan-ruled-out-of-second-t20i-against-new-zealand.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India's batting coach, Sitanshu Kotak, addressed the injury situation while speaking to reporters on the eve of the match. Kotak explained that the injury had already impacted the team's strategy during the first T20I, leading to the promotion of Tilak Varma to the No. 3 spot and Shreyas Iyer in the batting order. &quot;There was a lot of speculation I have also seen, just because Ishan had a strain in his groin, the batting order was changed,&quot; Kotak said. He further admitted on Friday that it was unlikely Kishan would be fit in time for the Saturday match.</p><p>The absence of Kishan has opened the door for Vaibhav Sooryavanshi to potentially join the starting XI. Sooryavanshi, who remained on the bench throughout the T20I series against the West Indies and the opening game against New Zealand, is considered a &quot;strong contender&quot; for the spot. Kotak mentioned that if Kishan does not recover completely, Sooryavanshi could definitely step in, although the coach refused to confirm the final selection before receiving clearance from the medical team.</p><p>This potential inclusion marks a shift in the team's recent stance. Previously, India captain Shreyas Iyer had dismissed suggestions of Sooryavanshi taking an opening spot, citing the consistent run-scoring of Abhishek Sharma and Sanju Samson. Iyer had suggested that the experience of being with the squad overseas would prepare Sooryavanshi for future conditions. However, the current injury crisis may force a change in the management's approach. Kotak noted that the final decision rests on the medical team’s advice regarding Kishan’s recovery status before the second match begins.</p><p>What to watch: The official team sheet on Saturday to see if Vaibhav Sooryavanshi makes his T20I debut at Hagley Oval.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source material, correctly identifying the BCCI statement and the context surrounding the player injury and potential replacement.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/new-zealand-vs-india-2026-27/ishan-kishan-ruled-out-of-2nd-t20i-against-new-zealand-door-opens-for-vaibhav-sooryavanshi-12223583#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
