     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kerala High Court Denies Stay on Waqf Board Reconstitution</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Division Bench of the Kerala High Court, comprising Justices Devan Ramachandran and Basant Balaji, has refused to stay the recent reconstitution of the Kerala State Waqf Board. The court rejected appeals filed by former chairperson K.S. Hamza and member C.K. Usman Haji, noting that the new board has already assumed charge.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/kerala-high-court-denies-stay-on-waqf-board-reconstitution.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The court directed the petitioners to issue formal notices to the current board members, with proceedings scheduled to resume on October 29. The Division Bench reviewed the matter following a Single Bench order that also declined to grant an interim stay on the reconstitution process.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all necessary details from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/kerala-hc-division-bench-refuses-to-stay-reconstitution-of-state-waqf-board/article71615934.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
