       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Southern Railway Conducts Public Outreach During Special Campaign 6.0</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Thiruvananthapuram Division of Southern Railway hosted 'Rail Jan Samvaad' at 102 stations to gather passenger feedback on service improvements. These sessions facilitated direct dialogue between railway officials, passengers, and stakeholders regarding cleanliness, punctuality, safety, and amenities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/southern-railway-conducts-public-outreach-during-special-cam.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This initiative is part of the broader Special Campaign 6.0, running from October 2 to 31 across Indian Railways. The campaign emphasizes swachhata, space utilization, and scrap disposal. In addition to public consultations, the division conducted cleanliness drives and tree planting events to promote greener railway premises while documenting specific passenger concerns for departmental follow-up action.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the outreach program and its objectives without padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Thiruvananthapuram/rail-jan-samvaad-organised-at-stations-to-promote-passenger-focused-service-improvements/article71616574.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
