       <h1>Stock Market Live: Nifty MidCap, SmallCap Decline</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Stock Market</span> <span>#Nifty</span> <span>#MidCap</span> <span>#SmallCap</span></div>
       <p>In Friday's live stock market updates, broader markets experienced declines, with key indices recording losses. This trend was observed across the Nifty segments, as reported by Business Standard.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/stock-market-live-nifty-midcap-smallcap-decline.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Nifty MidCap index registered a fall of 0.48 per cent during the trading session. This movement reflects a dip in the performance of medium-sized companies within the Indian stock market.</p><p>Similarly, the Nifty SmallCap index saw a more pronounced decline, dropping by 1.03 per cent. The performance of small-cap stocks often indicates broader market sentiment and risk appetite among investors.</p><p>What to watch: The performance of these broader market indices in the upcoming trading sessions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the provided market data and maintains an objective tone.</p>
