       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-23 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Tulluru PHC medical officer arrested for bribery</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Anti-Corruption Bureau officials in Guntur trapped Dr. D. Srinivas, a medical officer at Tulluru Primary Health Centre, while he was allegedly accepting a ₹25,000 bribe. The officer had demanded the payment to submit a favourable report regarding an employee who had received a show-cause notice for unauthorised absence.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-23/tulluru-phc-medical-officer-arrested-for-bribery.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following the trap, the ACB confirmed that an investigation into the incident is currently under way. The medical officer remains under scrutiny as officials process the evidence collected at the health centre.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all relevant facts from the source without filler.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/acb-traps-tulluru-phc-medical-officer-while-accepting-25000-bribe/article71617245.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
